            <ArticleTitle>Cisplatin-associated thrombosis.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>927-9</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1097/CAD.0b013e3283100e9c</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The discovery of cisplatin has made arguably the biggest contribution to cancer medicine, providing the basis for the chemotherapy treatment of many malignancies. In addition to well-documented toxicities such as neurotoxicity, cisplatin-induced vascular toxicity is becoming an increasing concern, with some authors describing it in up to 12% of patients. Given the efficacy of cisplatin, vascular toxicity represents a significant survivorship issue. We describe different manifestations of cisplatin-associated thrombosis and its putative pathophysiology.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
